      "analyzes" : {
        "type" : "literal",
        "value" : "mardi:Q6825953 || Cyclic tridiagonal solver via Sherman-Morrison rank-1 update || Reduces a cyclic tridiagonal system to a standard tridiagonal solve plus a low-rank correction using the Sherman-Morrison formula; retains O(n) structure while handling periodic boundary conditions. || mardi:Q127020 <|> mardi:Q6825862 || BiConjugate Gradient (BiCG) for nonsymmetric sparse linear systems || Extends CG to nonsymmetric matrices by building polynomial approximations in bi-orthogonal Krylov subspaces; may suffer irregular convergence, often superseded by stabilized variants like BiCGSTAB. || mardi:Q127020 <|> mardi:Q6825773 || Gauss-Jordan elimination to compute reduced row-echelon form and matrix inverses || Row-reduction with both forward elimination and full back-elimination to produce RREF and, optionally, A^{-1} by augmenting with the identity. Robust pivoting strategies are essential; numerical stability is generally inferior to LU with partial pivoting for solving Ax=b. This method is pedagogically transparent but rarely used in production solvers for dense systems. || mardi:Q127020 <|> mardi:Q6825760 || Classical Gaussian elimination with pivoting plus back-substitution for dense linear systems || Forward elimination transforms A to an upper-triangular U using row operations and (usually) partial pivoting; back-substitution then solves Ux=b. This is the workhorse of dense linear algebra and forms the basis for LU factorization used by LAPACK and most libraries. || mardi:Q127020 <|> mardi:Q6825618 || Thomas algorithm (tridiagonal matrix algorithm) for O(n) solution of tridiagonal systems || Performs a forward sweep eliminating subdiagonal entries followed by back substitution, exploiting the tridiagonal pattern for linear-time work and storage. Stable for diagonally dominant or SPD problems; otherwise pivoting may be needed. || mardi:Q127020 <|> mardi:Q6825600 || Björck-Pereyra O(n^2) algorithm for solving Vandermonde systems || Exploits the special structure of Vandermonde matrices to reduce work and improve numerical behavior compared to naive Gaussian elimination; useful in polynomial interpolation contexts. || mardi:Q127020 <|> mardi:Q6825578 || Generalized Minimal Residual || Builds an orthonormal Krylov basis via Arnoldi and chooses the iterate with minimal residual over the subspace; restarted and flexible variants control memory and cost. Robust and widely applicable with suitable preconditioning. || mardi:Q127020 <|> mardi:Q6825529 || Conjugate Gradient (CG) for sparse symmetric positive definite systems || Krylov subspace method minimizing the A-norm of the error; per-iteration cost is O(nnz) and convergence depends on κ(A) and preconditioning quality. Cornerstone solver for large SPD problems arising from PDEs. || mardi:Q127020 <|> mardi:Q6825507 || LU decomposition with (partial) pivoting for solving Ax=b and computing determinants || Factorizes a nonsingular matrix A into PA = LU with a permutation P, unit-lower L, and upper-triangular U. Once factored, multiple right-hand sides and determinants are efficient, and the factorization is more stable than naive Gauss-Jordan. || mardi:Q127020 <|> mardi:Q6825417 || Gaussian/LU factorization specialized to band-diagonal matrices || Stores only the populated diagonals and performs band-aware elimination with reduced fill and operation count proportional to the bandwidth. Common in PDE discretizations where the bandwidth is modest relative to n. || mardi:Q127020 <|> mardi:Q6825339 || Cholesky (LL^T) factorization for SPD matrices || For SPD matrices A=LL^T (or A=R^TR), enabling fast solves and log-determinants; numerically stable and halves the floating-point work compared to LU for SPD problems. Forms the basis of many preconditioners. || mardi:Q127020 <|> mardi:Q6825326 || BiCGSTAB (stabilized BiCG) for improved smooth convergence on nonsymmetric systems || Enhances BiCG by introducing a stabilization (minimal residual) step to reduce oscillatory behavior; widely used with ILU-type preconditioners. || mardi:Q127020"
